What\n\nThe staging aggregator's embed-at-promotion step (#5669 aggregator slice; the sequenced remainder of #1518 after the definition in #10350 and the item writer in #10788):\n\n- **`atlas_core::aggregate::embed_unit_into_shard`** — reads one staging unit's `items` + `chunks_raw`, embeds every chunk document-side with the mandated model, writes one new local core scan shard (`atlas-core-<tier>-<topic>-<nn>.db` with the exact `chunks` / vec-table / `atlas_manifest` schema shard discovery and the fan-out scan already read), stamps the unit DB's `atlas_manifest` `embedding_model`, and promotes the unit through `Registry::promote` — whose M6 gate (#7648, now closed) re-reads the stamp. No new read path: promoted entries are searchable by the existing fan-out.\n- **`DocEmbedder`** (embed.rs) — the document-side twin of `QueryEmbedder`: prompt-free, stored as produced, per the corpus contract in embed.rs's module docs. `AtlasEmbedder::embed_doc_raw` + `FixedDocEmbedder` included.\n- **`atlas-stage promote`** CLI verb — production wiring: builds the real embedder with the same model/ORT resolution as the atlas-search binary (ATLAS_MODEL_DIR / ATLAS_ORT_LIB, state-dir / HF-cache snapshots), loud failure when absent.\n- Chunk sensitivity is written in the scan vocabulary via the tier mapping (`shareable`/`personal`/`secret-bearing`, the inverse of `TierCeiling::from_sensitivity`), so an internal unit's chunks are admitted under the default personal ceiling.\n\nFailure shape: embed/write failures before the stamp remove any partial shard and leave the unit open; the stamp closes the staging DB to further `stage_artifact` writes (exact v1 table-set check), matching merge-on-close.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New oracle suite `crates/atlas-core/tests/aggregate.rs` (3 tests): promotion of a staged unit (DNS config + prose) into a shard that `open_from_spec(\"dir:…\")` discovers and `fanout_scan` ranks correctly (DNS chunk first for a DNS-shaped query); the registry gate refuses before the aggregator runs; empty-unit and second-run refusals; tier→sensitivity mapping.\n- `cargo test -p atlas-core -p atlas-search`: all green (126 lib tests + every integration suite, incl. the 3 new ones). `cargo fmt` applied to the touched files only.\n- Clippy via the shared broker target dir fails with a pre-existing rustc-version mismatch in cached crates (E0514 on serde/serde_json/sha2) — environment artifact, not this change; CI for this workspace is tests-only.\n\n## Remaining on #1518 (recorded, sequenced)\n\nLive promotion run against the real model + retrieval proof on #1518, shard-size benchmarks, and closing/linking #2469 — landing in the same task 17164 shift as follow-on steps after this PR merges (promotion needs the merged verb).\n\nRefs #1518, #5669. Part of task 17164.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797439782&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=10832&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F10832&signature=469dcda11a40f3176c4257e85a34e7c5420b296926eac1b556694dd7d82456d7\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/10832?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA",